== Effects ==
* Grants one {{E|Soul Heart}}.
* Enemy shots that hit Isaac have a 25% chance to be reflected.
** Isaac does not take damage from the reflected tears, but gets pushed a bit.
** The reflected tears are [[homing]] and [[Status Effects#Confusion|concussive]], and use Isaac's [[Damage]] and [[Tear effects]].
*** Projectiles that create other projectiles (e.g. {{E|Shady}}) can harm Isaac and be reflected.
** Can reflect:
*** {{dlc+|r}} Fireballs (e.g. from {{E|Crackle}}), but their lines of fire harm Isaac.{{dlc-}}
*** Fire projectiles (e.g. from {{E|Mega Satan}}).
*** {{dlc+|r}} Obstacles thrown by {{E|Polty}} or {{E|Kineti}}.{{dlc-}}
** Does not reflect:
*** Explosive projectiles (e.g. from {{E|Gurgle}}).
*** Lasers or beams.
*** {{dlc|r}}Lines of fire from fireballs.
*** {{dlc+|r}} Projectiles from {{E|Big Bony}}, {{E|Coal Boy}}, {{E|Danny}}.{{dlc-}}

== Interactions ==
* The following items that change the property of Isaac's tears affect the reflected tears:
** {{I|Eye of the Occult}}
** {{I|Haemolacria}}
** {{I|Ipecac}}
** {{I|Lachryphagy}}
** {{I|My Reflection}}
** {{I|Pop!}}
** {{I|Tiny Planet}}
** {{I|Trisagion}}
* The following items that modify Isaac's tears do not affect the reflected tears, aside from stat changes (if present):
** {{I|Brimstone}}
** {{I|Chocolate Milk}}
** {{I|C Section}}
** {{I|Cursed Eye}}
** {{I|Dr. Fetus}}
** {{I|Epic Fetus}}
** {{I|The Ludovico Technique}}
** {{I|Mom's Knife}}
** {{I|Monstro's Lung}}
** {{I|Neptunus}}
** {{I|Spirit Sword}}
** {{I|Technology}}
** {{I|Tech X}}
* {{I|20/20}} / {{C|Keeper}} and other multi-shot effects: Do not add the reflected tears.
* {{I|Anti-Gravity}} / {{I|Tractor Beam}}: Does not affect the reflected tears, aside from stat changes.
* {{I|Cone Head}}: Metal Plate's chance of reflecting effect is applied first.
** This leaves Isaac 40% chance to negate tears in any way.
* {{I|Dead Eye}}: The reflected tears grant the damage multiplier, but do not reset it even when they miss.
* {{I|Eye of Greed}} / {{I|Lead Pencil}}: The reflected tears are not counted for shots fired.
* {{I|Gnawed Leaf}}: Tears can be blocked while Isaac is invulnerable.
** This leaves Isaac 62.5% chance to negate tears in any way.
* {{I|Hallowed Ground}}: Metal Plate's chance of blocking effect is applied first.
* {{I|Infamy}}: Infamy's chance of blocking effect is applied first. Tears blocked by Infamy are not reflected by Metal Plate.
** This leaves Isaac 62.5% chance to negate tears in any way.
* {{I|Isaac's Heart}}: Tears can be blocked when hitting the heart, not Isaac.
* {{P|Holy Card}} / {{i|Holy Mantle}}: Metal Plate's chance of blocking projectiles is applied before the shield, allowing it to be saved.
* {{I|Host Hat}}: Host Hat's chance of blocking effect is applied first. Tears blocked by Host Hat are not reflected by Metal Plate.
** This leaves Isaac 40% chance to negate tears in any way.
* '''Metal Plate''': Additional copies of this item, such as from {{I|Diplopia}} / {{I|Crooked Penny}}, have no effect.

